    "topic": "hiring",
    "title": "California New Employee Registry Reporting Requirements for Employers",
    "summary": "Employers must report all new or rehired employees to California's New Employee Registry (NER) within 20 calendar days of the employee's start-of-work date. A rehire must be reported if the employee was separated from the employer for at least 60 consecutive days. Employers filing electronically must submit two monthly reports no less than 12 days and no more than 16 days apart. Failure to report may result in a $24 penalty per unreported employee, or $490 if non-reporting is an intentional agreement between employer and employee.",
