    "state": "CA",
    "topic": "termination",
    "title": "California Termination Pay Timing and WARN Notice Requirements",
    "summary": "Discharged employees must be paid all wages immediately at termination; employees who quit with at least 72 hours notice must be paid at the time of quitting, while those who quit without notice must be paid within 72 hours. Employers with 75 or more employees planning a layoff of 50 or more employees within a 30-day period, a plant closure, or a relocation of at least 100 miles must provide written notice at least 60 days in advance under California WARN. Notices must go to affected employees, the EDD, the Local Workforce Development Area, and the chief elected official of affected local government. Starting in 2026, WARN notices must also describe how employers will support laid-off workers.",
