    "title": "California Minimum Wage and Overtime Rules for Employers",
    "summary": "Effective January 1, 2026, California's minimum wage is $16.90 per hour for all employers not covered by a higher industry or local rate. Overtime is paid at 1.5 times the regular rate for hours over 8 in a workday (up to 12) and over 40 in a workweek, and double time for hours over 12 in a workday; the seventh consecutive workday also triggers overtime. Employers cannot use employee tips as a credit toward the minimum wage obligation, and employees cannot waive their right to overtime pay.",
