    "state": "DE",
    "topic": "state_programs",
    "title": "Delaware Paid Leave and EARNS Retirement Savings Programs",
    "summary": "Delaware operates two employer programs. Delaware Paid Leave requires most employers with 10 or more employees to provide paid family and medical leave, funded by less than 1% of an employee's weekly salary, with employees receiving up to 80% of wages (capped at $900 per week); contributions began January 1, 2025, and claims began January 1, 2026. Delaware EARNS is a state-sponsored Roth IRA savings program mandatory for private-sector employers with 5 or more W-2 employees who have operated at least 6 months and offer no qualified retirement plan; it is free to employers.",
