    "summary": "Florida's minimum wage will be $14.00 per hour effective September 30, 2025, rising to $15.00 per hour on September 30, 2026. Florida has no separate state overtime law; employers follow the federal FLSA, which requires overtime pay at one and one-half times the regular rate for hours worked in excess of 40 in a workweek. Overtime cannot be waived by agreement, and averaging hours over two or more weeks is not permitted. Employers must display required state and federal wage posters where employees can easily view them.",
