    "summary": "Hawaii is generally an at-will state, meaning employers do not need to give a reason to terminate an employee. Exceptions apply when a contract or collective bargaining agreement requires notice of reason. Employers may not discharge or discriminate against employees solely due to garnishment, a compensable work injury, testifying under employment law, or a positive on-site drug or alcohol screening test. Employees who believe they were illegally terminated must file a complaint with the Wage Standards Division within 30 days of the action.",
