    "state": "HI",
    "topic": "leave",
    "title": "Hawaii Family Leave Law Coverage and Key Provisions",
    "summary": "The Hawaii Family Leave Law (HFLL) applies to employers with 100 or more employees for each working day during 20 or more calendar weeks in the current or preceding calendar year. Eligible employees must have at least six consecutive months of service. Employers who provide sick leave must permit employees to use up to 10 days of accrued and available sick leave for family leave purposes. Employees are entitled to a four-week period of family leave, and leave may be taken intermittently.",
