    "summary": "Resident individuals applying for an initial Hawaii insurance producer license must pass a state exam through Pearson Vue, get fingerprinted via Fieldprint using code HI-DCCA-INS, and submit a completed application and fee within 60 days of fingerprinting through the NIPR website. Fingerprinting is required once when submitting two applications simultaneously, but again if a second license is sought later. Agencies using a trade name must register it with the Business Registration Division and then submit Form NTA to the Insurance Licensing Branch for Commissioner approval.",
