    "summary": "Employers with employees working in Hawaii are subject to the Wage Standards Division's enforcement of state labor laws. Covered employees must be paid at least the statutory minimum wage, with overtime required after 40 hours worked in a workweek. Wages must be paid at least twice a month and within seven days after the end of each pay period. Minors working in Hawaii require a child labor certificate or work permit until age 18.",
