    "title": "Iowa New Hire Reporting Requirements for Employers",
    "summary": "Iowa employers are required by federal and state law to report newly hired and rehired employees to the Centralized Employee Registry (CER), a state computer database. The CER helps child support agencies locate parents who owe support and speed up income withholding payments. Reporting new hires also supports unemployment insurance integrity by triggering investigations when a reported new hire is simultaneously receiving UI benefits. Employers can find reporting instructions on the CER website.",
