    "summary": "Iowa does not have a state-mandated paid sick leave or paid family and medical leave program. Federal FMLA, enforced by the U.S. Department of Labor, entitles eligible employees of covered employers to up to 12 workweeks of unpaid, job-protected leave per year for qualifying family and medical reasons, or up to 26 workweeks for military caregiver leave. Private-sector employers with 50 or more employees in 20 or more workweeks are covered. Employees must have worked at least 12 months and logged at least 1,250 hours in the prior 12 months.",
