    "topic": "wage_hour",
    "title": "Iowa Minimum Wage and Overtime Pay Requirements",
    "summary": "Iowa's current minimum wage is $7.25 per hour. Tipped employees may be paid as little as $4.35 per hour if they earn $30 or more per month in tips, provided total wages plus tips average at least $7.25 per hour. Employers grossing at least $300,000 in annual sales generally must comply with the Iowa Minimum Wage Law. For overtime, Iowa directs workers to the federal Wage and Hour Division; under the FLSA, overtime is paid at one and one-half times the regular rate for hours worked beyond 40 in a workweek.",
