    "summary": "Idaho taxes business net income, not gross receipts. The 2025 corporate income tax rate is 5.3% on taxable income, but insurance agencies organized as LLCs, S corporations, or partnerships are typically pass-through entities — income flows to owners' personal returns rather than being taxed at the entity level. Idaho also offers an affected business entity (ABE) election allowing partnerships and S corporations to pay Idaho income tax at the entity level. Agencies should confirm their specific tax situation with a qualified tax professional.",
