    "summary": "Maryland employers are required to obtain workers' compensation insurance from any licensed insurance company or from the Chesapeake Employers' Insurance Company. Employers may also apply to become self-insured with prior approval from the Workers' Compensation Commission. Employers who fail to secure coverage may be fined up to $10,000, and corporate officers can be held personally liable. The entire cost of coverage must be borne by the employer; deducting any portion from employee wages is a misdemeanor.",
