    "topic": "at_will",
    "title": "Maine At-Will Termination Rules and Key Exceptions",
    "summary": "In Maine, an employer can fire an employee without notice or cause, as long as there is no illegal discrimination. However, employers may not fire a worker due to illegal discrimination, refusal to perform an unsafe job, reporting an unsafe condition, being called for jury duty, having wages garnished, or filing a workers' compensation claim. A union contract may also limit termination to specific reasons, in which case the contract terms must be followed.",
