    "summary": "Maine imposes a graduated corporate income tax on entities organized as corporations with Maine-source income, with rates ranging from 3.5% (for income up to $350,000) to 8.93% (for income in excess of $3,500,000). S corporations are generally exempt unless the corporation has federal taxable income at the corporate level. Insurance companies subject to Maine's premiums tax are not subject to the corporate income tax. Agencies should consult a tax professional to determine how these rules apply to their specific situation.",
