    "summary": "Employers must report newly hired or rehired employees to Maine's Division of Support Enforcement and Recovery (DSER) within 7 days of the date of hire. Independent contractors must be reported when anticipated reimbursement equals or exceeds $2,500 in a year. Employers who fail to comply are subject to a civil penalty of up to $200 per month per violation. Multi-state employers may designate one state to receive all new hire reports rather than reporting to each state separately.",
