    "topic": "leave",
    "title": "Maine Earned Paid Leave and Paid Family Medical Leave Programs",
    "summary": "Maine's Earned Paid Leave law, effective January 1, 2021, requires employers with more than 10 employees in Maine for more than 120 days in a calendar year to provide paid leave. Employees accrue 1 hour of earned paid leave for every 40 hours worked, up to 40 hours per year, usable for any reason. Maine's separate Paid Family and Medical Leave (PFML) program allows eligible workers to apply for up to 12 weeks of paid leave per benefit year beginning May 2026, covering medical, parental, family care, military family, and safe leave.",
