    "title": "Missouri At-Will Termination Rules and Final Wage Requirements",
    "summary": "Missouri follows the Employment-At-Will doctrine, meaning either the employer or employee may end the employment relationship at any time and for any reason. Exceptions apply when an employment contract exists, when termination involves discrimination based on race, color, age, national origin, religion, ancestry, sex, or physical/mental disability, when merit laws apply, or when the state's limited public policy exception applies. Employers must pay all wages due at the time of dismissal. If not paid, the employer has seven days to respond to a certified written request, or may owe additional wages for up to sixty days.",
