    "topic": "at_will",
    "title": "New York At-Will Termination Rules and Employee Protections",
    "summary": "In New York, private-sector employers are not required to have good cause to fire an employee and may do so for unfair or no reason at all. However, employers cannot fire workers for illegal reasons, including discrimination based on race, religion, sex, age, disability, or other protected characteristics, retaliation for reporting labor-law violations, whistleblowing, union activity, filing workers' compensation claims, or taking protected leave. Fast-food workers in New York City cannot be fired or have hours reduced by more than 15 percent without just cause or a legitimate business reason. Employees are entitled to any outstanding wages no later than their next regular pay day.",
