    "summary": "New York corporations or businesses conducting certain activities in the state may owe an annual franchise tax under the New York State Tax Law. The tax calculation and return type depend on the business structure: general business corporations, S corporations, insurance corporations, and transportation or utility companies each file under different articles of the Tax Law. LLCs and LLPs, as well as partnerships, are addressed separately. An agency should consult a tax professional to determine its specific obligations and applicable rates.",
