    "summary": "All New York employers must report newly hired or rehired employees to the state within 20 calendar days of the hiring date. Required information includes employee name, address, Social Security number, hire date, employer identification details, and dependent health insurance availability. Employers must also report independent contractors with contracts exceeding $2,500, effective January 1, 2022. Penalties for failing to report are $20 per employee not reported or per false/incomplete report filed.",
