    "title": "New York Paid Sick Leave and Paid Family Leave Requirements",
    "summary": "New York requires employers with 100 or more employees to provide up to 56 hours of paid sick leave per year, and those with 5–99 employees to provide up to 40 hours. Employers with 0–4 employees must provide up to 40 hours of unpaid sick leave, or paid leave if net income exceeds $1 million. Leave accrues at no less than one hour per 30 hours worked. Separately, New York's Paid Family Leave program sets a 2026 maximum weekly benefit of $1,228.53, funded by an employee contribution rate of 0.432% of gross wages, up to an annual maximum of $411.91.",
