    "state": "OR",
    "topic": "business_tax",
    "title": "Oregon Corporation Excise, Income, and Corporate Activity Tax Structure",
    "summary": "Oregon imposes a corporation excise tax on businesses doing business in Oregon, measured by net income, and a separate Corporate Activity Tax (CAT) on commercial activity exceeding $1 million, computed as $250 plus 0.57 percent of taxable Oregon commercial activity above $1 million. C corporation excise tax filers pay the greater of calculated tax or minimum tax; calculated tax is 6.6 percent on Oregon taxable income of $1 million or less, or $66,000 plus 7.6 percent on amounts above $1 million. S corporations doing business in Oregon pay a $150 minimum excise tax; income flows to shareholders. Insurance agencies should consult a tax professional regarding their specific filing obligations.",
