    "summary": "South Carolina is an at-will state, meaning employers may terminate employees for any reason, a good reason, a bad reason, or no reason. Employees may also quit without providing notice for similar reasons. If an employee believes termination was due to discrimination based on race, color, age, sex, handicap or disability, national origin, or religion, they may contact the South Carolina Human Affairs Commission. Upon separation, employers must pay all wages due within 48 hours or the next regularly scheduled payday, not to exceed 30 days.",
