    "summary": "South Dakota does not impose a corporate income tax, meaning neither C corporations nor pass-through entities owe a state income-based business tax. Businesses are subject to other taxes such as sales and use tax, contractor's excise tax, bank franchise tax, and various excise taxes depending on their activity. Returns filed electronically are due by the 20th of each month following the reporting period, with payments due on the 25th. Insurance agencies should consult a tax professional to determine which specific tax types apply to their operations.",
