    "summary": "All South Dakota employers must report newly hired or rehired employees to the New Hire Reporting Center within 20 days of the first day of work. This applies to full-time, part-time, temporary, seasonal, and student workers. Rehired employees — those not paid for the past 30 days — must also be reported using their most recent hire date. Failure to comply may result in a $25 penalty per violation, or up to $500 per employee if there is a conspiracy to avoid reporting.",
