    "summary": "South Dakota does not operate a state paid family or medical leave program. Federal FMLA, administered by the U.S. Department of Labor, entitles eligible employees of covered employers to up to 12 workweeks of unpaid, job-protected leave per year for qualifying family and medical reasons, and up to 26 workweeks for military caregiver leave. Private-sector employers with 50 or more employees in 20 or more workweeks are covered; public agencies and local educational agencies are covered regardless of size. Employers must continue group health benefits during leave under the same terms.",
