    "summary": "Employers in South Dakota must register with the Reemployment Assistance Tax Unit, file quarterly wage reports, and pay payroll taxes that finance the state's reemployment assistance program. The taxable wage base for 2026 remains at $15,000. New non-construction employers pay a Year 1 RA Tax rate of 1.20%, dropping to 1.00% in Years 2 and 3 (with a positive balance), plus a 0.55% administrative fee. Construction employers pay 6.00% in Year 1 and 3.00% in Years 2 and 3. Quarterly reports are due by the last day of the month following each quarter's end.",
