    "summary": "South Dakota workers' compensation law covers nearly all employers, with limited exceptions. Exemptions include domestic servants (unless working more than 20 hours per calendar week and more than six weeks in any 13-week period), farm or agricultural labor, independent contractors, certain elected officials, and workfare participants. The source does not specify how coverage must be obtained or minimum employee-count thresholds beyond the domestic servant hours rule. Employers can verify coverage through the state's online Coverage Verification Service.",
