    "summary": "Washington is an at-will employment state, meaning employers may fire any employee at any time, for any or no reason, and are not required to give notice or warnings before terminating employment. However, employers cannot fire or retaliate against employees for exercising protected rights or filing complaints under certain employment laws. Protected areas include overtime, paid sick leave, safety complaints, discrimination, protected leave, and equal pay. Effective July 1, 2025, additional protections apply when employers use immigration-related threats to discourage workers from exercising workplace rights.",
