    "title": "Washington Paid Sick Leave and Paid Family Medical Leave",
    "summary": "Washington employers must provide paid sick leave, accruing at a minimum of one hour for every 40 hours worked, paid at the employee's normal hourly rate. Employees may begin using leave 90 calendar days after their first day of work, and unused balances of 40 hours or less must carry over each year. As of July 27, 2025, paid sick leave may also be used to prepare for or participate in immigration proceedings. Washington also offers a Paid Family and Medical Leave program for workers facing serious health conditions, family caregiving, bonding, or military-related needs.",
